{
	title: 'OpenCode Go: /login opencode',
	spec: "OpenCode Go subscribers can use Hal. OpenCode Go is a gateway that authenticates with an API key (models.dev: opencode-go, env OPENCODE_API_KEY) and serves each model over one protocol under https://opencode.ai/inference/go: OpenAI Chat Completions (openai/v1/chat/completions), OpenAI Responses (openai/v1/responses), Anthropic Messages (anthropic/v1/messages) or Google Gemini (google/v1beta/models/<model>:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse). models.dev names a model's protocol by its provider.npm (@ai-sdk/openai: Responses, @ai-sdk/anthropic: Messages, @ai-sdk/google: Gemini; none: Chat Completions; a model models.dev does not list: Responses, which the gateway serves for every non-Gemini model); the gateway's GET /v1/models does not. It is one more openai-compat endpoint: Chat Completions models use openai-compat.ts, and Responses or Messages models reuse the bodies and parsers of openai.ts and anthropic.ts, not new protocol clients. Provider-hosted web search is not offered through the gateway. Gemini models use gemini.ts, a body and parser of the Gemini protocol, replaying each thoughtSignature on its part. `/login opencode` (alias opencode-go) asks for the key through a secret form question and stores it in this home's credentials file; OPENCODE_API_KEY also works (task nd's rule: stored login first). Requests of every protocol send User-Agent 'hal' and x-opencode-session with the session id, as the old Hal did (artifact old-openai.ts in task q7: compatHeaders); the gateway refuses requests without x-opencode-session. The model list comes from models.dev. Showing the subscription's usage (old Hal's opencode-usage.ts) is not part of this task. Each OpenCode Go key is an account (auth.ts Kind 'opencode-go'): /login opencode with a new key adds an entry to the credentials file's opencode-go array (the old single { apiKey } shape stays readable; the same key again adds nothing), and OPENCODE_API_KEY is the last account. Requests of every protocol rotate across them like Anthropic/OpenAI accounts: a 429 limits only that account, a 401 or no-credits sets it aside, /account switches, /status and INSPECT logins list each account with its rate limit.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"host/api-keys.ts keeps keys stored by /login in the credentials file as `<provider>: { apiKey }` (here 'opencode-go'), beside the anthropic logins; save() creates the file 0600 and bumps auth.state.logins so a session blocked on login retries. An entry without apiKey is corrupt and throws.",
		"Every openai-compat endpoint with keyEnv now looks for a stored key first (apiKeys.get(endpoint name)), then the variable. A missing key is failure 'auth', so the session blocks (reason names /login <Endpoint.login> and the variable) and resumes after the login instead of ending in error.",
		'Endpoint gained login (the /login argument named in messages), models: false (no GET /models: the picker falls back to modelsDev.ids, which works because the endpoint is named opencode-go like the models.dev id) and headers(req) (extra chat headers). ProviderRequest gained sessionId, which turns.runTurn passes, for x-opencode-session.',
		'./test also unsets OPENCODE_API_KEY. opencode.test.ts reuses the real opencode-go endpoint with baseUrl pointed at a fake server, so the headers under test are the shipped ones.',
		'Invariant: an opencode-go rate limit binds one account (limits key "opencode-go <account>"); an account-less legacy "opencode-go/<model>" limit, left by the single-key era, blocks no account (requests with an account check limits.on only). Accounts are named by email if any, else "account N"; none is a subscription, so pickAccount keeps file order.',
		'Invariant: an opencode-go model goes to the protocol models.dev names for it (ModelInfo.npm from provider.npm), with the picked account key (Bearer, or x-api-key for Messages). Sending every model to Chat Completions made grok-4.7 and muse-spark-* fail with HTTP 400 ModelProtocolUnsupported. HttpRequest.parse lets one provider parse each request with its protocol parser. Until the models.dev cache has npm (refreshed at each start), every model takes Chat Completions. Thinking from opencode-go turns is not replayed (its blocks carry provider opencode-go). Checked by hand 2026-10-23: grok-4.7 and muse-spark-1.2-contributor (Responses), glm-5.3 (Chat Completions) and minimax-m3 (Messages) answered a tool call and its result. The old https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1 base still lists models, but the docs list only inference/go.',
		'Invariant: a Gemini functionCall goes back with its thoughtSignature (stored as a signature event "gemini:<sig>" before the call), and a first functionCall without one carries skip_thought_signature_validator; otherwise Gemini 3 refuses the request. gemini-4-argon-contributor refuses Responses and Messages with ModelProtocolUnsupported; only the Google route works. Checked by hand: a tool call, its replay with the real signature, and foreign (signature-less) history all answered.',
		'Probed 2026-10-23: grok-4.6, glm-5.1, omen-alpha, kimi-k2.6, minimax-m2.5, qwen3.6-plus and qwen3.7-max are on the gateway (GET /v1/models) but not in models.dev; all take Responses, grok-4.6 only Responses, none Gemini. mimo-v2.5-pro (in models.dev) fails upstream on every route with "Upstream request failed: [400] Unsupported model": an OpenCode problem, shown whole.'
	],
	needs: ['nd', 'qq']
